subproblems.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ and U₁, U₂, W, V ⊆ ℝ^P. Let X ∈ D_{m+1}(U₁) and A ∈ D_{m+1}(U₂) be currents (GeometricCurrentOn). Assume:
- W is open and W ⊆ U₂;
- the closure of V is compact and closure V ⊆ W;
- (H) X(η) = A(η′) for every η ∈ D^{m+1}(U₁) and η′ ∈ D^{m+1}(U₂) with η(x) = η′(x) for every x ∈ V.
Then M(∂X) ≤ M_W(∂A). Here M(∂X) = M_{U₁}(∂X) is the mass of ∂X ∈ D_m(U₁), and M_W(∂A) is the mass in W of ∂A ∈ D_m(U₂). Both are the suprema of the current over test forms supported in the indicated set with Euclidean coefficient norm ≤ 1 everywhere (SimonGMT massOn).
